    "result": "Excellent! The fix is working perfectly. Both files are now created:\n\n\u2705 **FRAI-SPEC.md** - The specification template\n\u2705 **.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml** - The GitHub Actions workflow file (this was missing before)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI's `gate` command passed arguments to the `frai-gate` subprocess. The problem was in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n**Root cause:** The command definition used `[args...]` to capture positional arguments, but the `--ci` flag was not being passed through because Commander.js doesn't automatically include unknown options/flags in the variadic args array, even with `.allowUnknownOption(true)`.\n\n**Fix:** Instead of relying on Commander to parse and pass arguments, I now extract all arguments directly from `process.argv` after the `gate` keyword and pass them all through to `frai-gate`. This preserves all flags and options exactly as the user typed them.\n\nThe fix has been deployed and verified\u2014`frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both the spec file and the GitHub Actions workflow.",
